title: The key under the mat
story: fernhill
continues: arrival
description: The tarnished key is concealed on the doormat — invisible to
  reference until it is searched for, and worth the first five points.

---

# The mat's own description is the only clue: it "sits a little proud of the
# flagstone, as if something kept it from lying flat."
> examine the doormat
[OK: contains "It sits a little proud of the flagstone"]

# Concealed means unreferenceable, not merely unlisted — the key cannot be
# named at all before the search.
> take the tarnished key
[OK: contains "You can't see any such thing"]
[EVENT: false, type="if.event.taken"]

> search the doormat
[OK: contains "Hidden on the doormat, you discover: a tarnished key"]

# Turn 14 lands here: the long-night sequence moves the story to midnight.
# This is a function of how many turns `arrival` spent, not of this file.
[OK: contains "the last light goes out of the sky"]

> take the tarnished key
[OK: contains "You take the tarnished key from the doormat"]
[EVENT: true, type="if.event.taken"]
[STATE: true, player.inventory contains tarnished key]

# `score found worth 5`, awarded by the key's own `after taking it, once`.
> score
[OK: contains "You have scored 5 out of 50"]
[OK: contains "the rank of a Trespasser"]

> inventory
[OK: contains "tarnished key"]
[OK: contains "solicitor"]
